Commit:     welpy-cw <h.w.forms@arcor.de>
CommitDate: Mon Jun 22 14:20:31 2026 -0700

    Bug 2047364 - Remove nsIMailboxUrl XPCOM interface. r=mkmelin


    Like nsIPop3URL before it, nsIMailboxUrl carried request state (action,
    message key, message size, copy/move batch state, copy handler) on what
    should have been a plain URL. This prevented serialization across
    processes and went against necko's assumption that nsIURI is just a URL.

    Changes:
    - Delete nsIMailboxUrl.idl. nsMailboxUrl now inherits only
      nsMsgMailNewsUrl, nsIMsgMessageUrl, and nsIMsgI18NUrl.
    - Move nsMailboxAction constants to a scoped enum class
      MailboxAction in nsMailboxUrl.h (e.g. MailboxAction::FetchMessage).
    - nsMailboxService::PrepareMessageUrl now returns nsIMsgMailNewsUrl**;
      callers use static_cast<nsMailboxUrl*> for concrete method access.
    - nsMailboxProtocol::m_runningUrl changed from nsCOMPtr<nsIMailboxUrl>
      to RefPtr<nsMailboxUrl>; redundant do_QueryInterface calls replaced
      with direct pointer access.
    - nsMailboxService::CreatePop3URI now extracts the message key
      directly from the spec instead of querying the base URI.
    - Remove unused #include "nsIMailboxUrl.h" from nsMsgUtils.cpp,
      nsMessenger.cpp, and nsParseMailbox.cpp.
    - Devirtualize nsMailboxUrl methods that no longer implement any
      XPCOM interface (NS_IMETHOD → nsresult).
    - Update test_mailboxProtocol.js to remove nsIMailboxUrl QI.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D306600

